  "question": {
    "text": "The molar solubility(s) of zirconium phosphate with molecular formula $\\left(\\mathrm{Zr}^{4+}\\right)_3\\left(\\mathrm{PO}_4^{3-}\\right)_4$ is given by relation :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{sp}}}{9612}\\right)^{\\frac{1}{3}}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{sp}}}{6912}\\right)^{\\frac{1}{7}}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{sp}}}{8435}\\right)^{\\frac{1}{7}}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{sp}}}{5348}\\right)^{\\frac{1}{6}}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{array}{cc}\\mathrm{Zr}_3\\left(\\mathrm{PO}_4\\right)_4(\\mathrm{~s}) \\rightleftharpoons & 3 \\mathrm{Zr}^{+4}(\\mathrm{aq})+4 \\mathrm{PO}_4^{-3}(\\mathrm{aq}) \\\\ - & 3 \\mathrm{~s} \\quad 4 \\mathrm{~s}\\end{array}$\n\n\n\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{K}_{\\text {sp }}=(3 \\mathrm{~s})^3(4 \\mathrm{~s})^4=6912 \\mathrm{~s}^7 \\\\ & \\mathrm{~s}=\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{sp}}}{6912}\\right)^{1 / 7}\\end{aligned}$"
  }
